      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The term \"standard patient\" is used to describe the general characteristics that are common or expected in the majority of cases as presented in medical literature or textbooks. This is not to imply that there is a baseline physiological profile that others do not meet. Rather, it's an educational way to distinguish the commonly observed features of a condition across a diverse patient population. However, it's important to note that this classification doesn't diminish the uniqueness of individual experiences and presentations – every patient's case is valuable, even when diverging from typical presentations. Medical professionals strive to recognize variability and ensure that all patients, regardless of demographic, receive accurate diagnoses and appropriate care.",
